# Line endings are pinned, not left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# The build runs on Linux and every generator in scripts/ writes LF. On a Windows
# clone (autocrlf=true) the pages came out CRLF, and patchHreflang's matcher — which
# only allowed \n between <link rel="alternate"> tags — stopped matching after the
# first line. It then appended a fresh block instead of replacing the old one, giving
# 8,558 pages duplicate hreflang alternates the first time the build ran locally.
# CI never saw it because CI is Linux.
#
# The matcher is now CRLF-tolerant as well, but the generated site is LF everywhere
# so that a local build and a CI build produce byte-identical output.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
